                                                                                                         sio:SIO_000516
                                                                                                         sio:SIO_000539) ; 
                                                                a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>].
sio:SIO_000512 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "SIO_000512";
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A line segment is a line and a part of a curve that is (inclusively) bounded by two terminal points."@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://semanticscience.org/ontology/sio.owl>;
               rdfs:label "line segment"@en;
               rdfs:subClassOf [<http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> ":arc758fb238" ; 
                                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onClass> sio:SIO_000532 ; 
                                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#qualifiedCardinality> "2"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> sio:SIO_000369 ; 
                                a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                               sio:SIO_000511.
sio:SIO_000513 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "SIO_000513";
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A tick mark is a line segment that is spatially positioned perpendicular to the axis of a statistical graph and indicates the position of a specific numeric value (which may be indicated by an adjacent value label) on a value axis, or is one of a pair of tick marks that delineates the boundary of a categorical value (which may be indicated by an adjacent category label) on the categorical axis."@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://semanticscience.org/ontology/sio.owl>;
               rdfs:label "tick mark"@en;
               rdfs:subClassOf sio:SIO_000512.
sio:SIO_000514 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "SIO_000514";
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A major tick mark is a tick mark that indicates the position of a specific numeric value and is adjacent to its value label on the value axis, or is one of a pair of tick marks that delineates the boundary of a categorical value indicated by an adjacent category label on the categorical axis."@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://semanticscience.org/ontology/sio.owl>;
               rdfs:label "major tick mark"@en;
               rdfs:subClassOf sio:SIO_000513.
sio:SIO_000515 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "SIO_000515";
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A minor tick mark is a tick mark that indicates the position of a specific numeric value but has no adjacent value label, or is one of a pair of tick marks that delineates the boundary of a categorical value but has no adjacent category label on the categorical axis."@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://semanticscience.org/ontology/sio.owl>;
               rdfs:label "minor tick mark"@en;
               rdfs:subClassOf sio:SIO_000513.
sio:SIO_000516 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "SIO_000516";
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A ray is a line which that is bounded by a startpoint and extends outwards infinitely along one dimension."@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://semanticscience.org/ontology/sio.owl>;
               rdfs:label "ray"@en;
               rdfs:subClassOf sio:SIO_000511.
sio:SIO_000517 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "SIO_000517";
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A quadrilateral is a polygon with composed of four points and four line segments, in which each point is fully connected to two other points."@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://semanticscience.org/ontology/sio.owl>;
               rdfs:label "quadrilateral"@en;
               rdfs:subClassOf sio:SIO_000505.
sio:SIO_000518 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "SIO_000518";
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A rectangle is a quadrilateral in which one pair of line segments are  parallel and the other pair are perpendicular to the first pair."@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://semanticscience.org/ontology/sio.owl>;
               rdfs:label "rectangle"@en;
               rdfs:subClassOf sio:SIO_000517.
sio:SIO_000519 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "SIO_000519";
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A bar is a rectangle that is located in the plot of a statistical graph in which its length is proportional to the values that it represents."@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://semanticscience.org/ontology/sio.owl>;
               rdfs:label "bar"@en;
               rdfs:subClassOf sio:SIO_000518.
sio:SIO_000520 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "SIO_000520";
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A triangle is a polygon composed of three points and three line segments, in which each point is fully connected to another point along through the line segment."@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://semanticscience.org/ontology/sio.owl>;
               rdfs:label "triangle"@en;
               rdfs:subClassOf sio:SIO_000505.
sio:SIO_000521 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "SIO_000521";
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> """A directed line segment is a line segment that is contained by an ordered pair 
of endpoints (a start point and an endpoint)."""@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://semanticscience.org/ontology/sio.owl>;
               rdfs:label "directed line segment"@en;
               rdfs:subClassOf [<http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> ":arc758fb240" ; 
                                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onClass> sio:SIO_000509 ; 
                                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#qualifiedCardinality> "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> sio:SIO_000369 ; 
                                a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                               [<http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> ":arc758fb239" ; 
                                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onClass> sio:SIO_000508 ; 
                                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#qualifiedCardinality> "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> sio:SIO_000369 ; 
                                a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                               sio:SIO_000512.
sio:SIO_000522 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "SIO_000522";
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "An arrowed line is a directed line segment in which one or both endpoints is tangentially part of a triangle that bisects the line."@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://semanticscience.org/ontology/sio.owl>;
               rdfs:label "arrowed line segment"@en;
               rdfs:subClassOf [<http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> ":arc758fb242" ; 
                                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onClass> sio:SIO_000520 ; 
                                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#maxQualifiedCardinality> "2"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> sio:SIO_000369 ; 
                                a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                               [<http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> ":arc758fb241" ; 
                                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> sio:SIO_000520 ; 
                                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> sio:SIO_000028 ; 
                                a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                               sio:SIO_000521.
sio:SIO_000523 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "SIO_000523";
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A single arrowed line is directed line in which the endpoint is tangentially part of a triangle that bisects the line."@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://semanticscience.org/ontology/sio.owl>;
               rdfs:label "single arrowed line segment"@en;
               rdfs:subClassOf [<http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> ":arc758fb243" ; 
                                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onClass> sio:SIO_000520 ; 
                                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#qualifiedCardinality> "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> sio:SIO_000369 ; 
                                a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                               sio:SIO_000522;
               <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> sio:SIO_000524.
sio:SIO_000524 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "SIO_000524";
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A double arrowed line is an arrowed line in which both terminal points are  tangentially part of different triangles that bisect the line."@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://semanticscience.org/ontology/sio.owl>;
               rdfs:label "double arrowed line segment"@en;
               rdfs:subClassOf [<http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> ":arc758fb244" ; 
                                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onClass> sio:SIO_000520 ; 
                                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#qualifiedCardinality> "2"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> sio:SIO_000369 ; 
                                a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                               sio:SIO_000522.
sio:SIO_000525 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "SIO_000525";
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A horizontal line is a line that is positionally oriented with the horizon."@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://semanticscience.org/ontology/sio.owl>;
               rdfs:label "horizontal line"@en;
               rdfs:subClassOf sio:SIO_000534.
sio:SIO_000526 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "SIO_000526";
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A vertical line is a line that is positionally oriented perpendicular to the horizon."@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://semanticscience.org/ontology/sio.owl>;
               rdfs:label "vertical line"@en;
               rdfs:subClassOf sio:SIO_000534.
sio:SIO_000527 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "SIO_000527";
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A trend line is a line, line segment or ray that is part of a statistical graph which indicates a statistical or visual direction across categorical or value data."@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://semanticscience.org/ontology/sio.owl>;
               rdfs:label "trend line"@en;
               rdfs:subClassOf sio:SIO_000535.
sio:SIO_000528 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "SIO_000528";
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "An increasing line is a line segment in which the startpoint and endpoint are ordered along one dimension and the difference of values in a second dimension is positive."@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://semanticscience.org/ontology/sio.owl>;
               rdfs:label "increasing line"@en;
               rdfs:subClassOf sio:SIO_000527.
sio:SIO_000529 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "SIO_000529";
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "An decreasing line is a line segment in which the startpoint and endpoint are ordered along one dimension and the difference of values in a second dimension is negative."@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://semanticscience.org/ontology/sio.owl>;
               rdfs:label "decreasing line"@en;
               rdfs:subClassOf sio:SIO_000527.
sio:SIO_000530 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "SIO_000530";
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "An plateau line is a line segment in which the startpoint and endpoint are ordered along one dimension and the difference of values in a second dimension is zero."@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://semanticscience.org/ontology/sio.owl>;
               rdfs:label "plateau line"@en;
               rdfs:subClassOf sio:SIO_000527.
sio:SIO_000531 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "SIO_000531";
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A drop line is a statistical graph line that vertically or horizontally connects a data series line with a value axis in a statistical graph."@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://semanticscience.org/ontology/sio.owl>;
               rdfs:label "drop line"@en;
               rdfs:subClassOf sio:SIO_000535.
sio:SIO_000532 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "SIO_000532";
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A terminal point is a point that defines the finite extension of a line."@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
