               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A hard disk drive (HDD) is a non-volatile, random access device for digital data. It features rotating rigid platters on a motor-driven spindle within a protective enclosure. Data is magnetically read and written on the platter by read/write heads that float on a film of air above the platters."@en;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://semanticscience.org/ontology/sio.owl>;
